; Leg HB -- the Victor SENDS 32,768 bytes BY NAME.  Edit 16 range.
;
; BENCH take-file: there is no "set line" here.  ~/.kermrc names the adapter.
; CHECK THAT IT NAMES THE ONE THAT IS PLUGGED IN.
;
; NOTE THE DIRECTION.  The host RECEIVES, so START THIS FIRST -- the Victor
; is the initiator and gives up if nothing answers its S packets.
;
; CONTROL: SS16ai leg CC -- PX_CAU exactly (32 values), 4,512 prefixes,
; 37,557 wire bytes, 18 packets, 22.207 s, 1,475 cps.
;
; THIS IS A COUNTING LEG.  Quote the wire-byte count as the result and the
; cps as an illustration: CC and CD were 1.397 s apart against a bench floor
; of ~1.3 s.  Read the "prefixing policy" line out of pktstat.py.
;
; AND IT MUST BE BYTE-EXACT.  PX_CAU puts control characters on the wire raw
; -- the whole point of it and the only way it can go wrong.
;
; Edit 16's failure signature is an error line with an EMPTY ck_errstr().
; SS16ah leg BS produced no error line at all.  This is the edit's fourth
; end-to-end confirmation and its second on hardware.
;
; READ IT WITH:
;     python3 v9k/tools/pktstat.py --rxbytes <from STEPHB.OUT> s16bcHB.pkt
; Residual -11 clean, +28 with a startup timeout.
; cmp FIRST, then the counters.  A leg that is fast and wrong is the failure.

set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
set retry 30
log packets s16bcHB.pkt
receive gothb.dat
statistics
